{"type":"message","id":"05bd36ec","parentId":"9567f452","timestamp":"2026-03-13T18:39:20.204Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\nWait, why did it run all 17 sites? Oh right, because the crawler-node.js is still loading the default config, not the test one I passed? Because the --config parameter might not be implemented. Let's check the crawler-node.js code to see how it loads config. Let's read the first part of it.\nWait, also, the test config I created only has 3 sites, but it ran 17, so it's definitely using the default urls.json instead of the test one. So I need to modify the crawler temporarily to use urls-test.json, or create a test script that uses the test config. Alternatively, just rename urls.json to urls.tmp, rename urls-test.json to urls.json, run the crawler, then rename back. Oh that's easier. Let's do that.\nFirst, mv urls.json urls.tmp, then mv urls-test.json urls.json, run the crawler, then mv back urls.tmp to urls.json, and urls.json.bak is already the backup, so that's safe.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8g2m9bo5bbct64fz8cf6cc04","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/yankeeting/.openclaw/workspace/projects/daily-news-crawler/config && mv urls.json urls.tmp && mv urls-test.json urls.json"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"volces-com","model":"ark-code-latest","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773427155210}}
